            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Move 1" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(rsig)
                <div class="r-two" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr">
                    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.4cqw">
                        <p class="r-kick">move 01, the product</p>
                        <h4 class="r-h">Make the product <em>the celebrity.</em></h4>
                        <div class="r-rule"></div>
                        <p class="r-lede">Glossier You outlived Glossier’s hype because people love the bottle, not the founder. Rhode needs its own: the peptide lip treatment and the lip case, marketed as icons that don’t need Hailey in the shot.</p>
                    </div>
                    <ul class="r-list">
                        <li class="r-card" style="--n: 0"><b>Hero first:</b> every campaign leads with the product, not the face</li>
                        <li class="r-card" style="--n: 1"><b>Own a word:</b> “glazed” as a look anyone can get</li>
                        <li class="r-card" style="--n: 2"><b>Fewer launches:</b> one new icon a year, not a full makeup line</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Move 2" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(rsig)
                <div class="r-two" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr">
                    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.4cqw">
                        <p class="r-kick">move 02, the faces</p>
                        <h4 class="r-h">Build a bench <em>of faces.</em></h4>
                        <div class="r-rule"></div>
                        <p class="r-lede">Eight new countries in 2026 is the perfect excuse. Sign a local face for every market (Mexico City, Lisbon, Prague) and a creator program at home, so Hailey becomes the founder, not the only face.</p>
                    </div>
                    <ul class="r-list">
                        <li class="r-card" style="--n: 0"><b>One muse per market,</b> chosen by local fans</li>
                        <li class="r-card" style="--n: 1"><b>A paid creator bench</b> for every routine</li>
                        <li class="r-card" style="--n: 2"><b>Hailey in fewer posts,</b> with sales tracked per face</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Move 3" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(rsig)
                <div class="r-two" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr">
                    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.4cqw">
